# raw/fonts/ is a CACHE, not a source: tools/fonts.py downloads each Google
# subset it cuts from and stores it here (tools/fonts.py:160), so a missing
# file is one command away. raw/img/ stays tracked on purpose — its Figma
# links have expired (tools/optimize.py:11) and icon-eye.svg was repaired by
# hand there, so those bytes are the only copy.
